orkflows","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fPWjWTFveBQ","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/synthetic-monitoring-explained-a-guide-to-reliable-devops-workflows-4gstmmnor","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/fPWjWTFveBQ/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-03T11:01:00.000Z"},{"id":"pzWIEAlw4","title":"How RAG, GraphRAG, and Context Engineering Improve AI Performance","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pN-LfxNFiTc","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-rag-graphrag-and-context-engineering-improve-ai-performance-pzwiealw4","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/pN-LfxNFiTc/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-02T11:01:22.000Z"},{"id":"hDMPuySB6","title":"Granite 4.1, IBM Bob & building a quantum ecosystem","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zk3FX8ZXa-s","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/granite-4-1-ibm-bob-building-a-quantum-ecosystem-hdmpuysb6","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Zk3FX8ZXa-s/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-01T10:01:04.000Z"},{"id":"xDJEDWwmp","title":"Q\u2011Day Explained: How Quantum Computing Threatens Today\u2019s Cryptography","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rTM95-gZtOs","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/q-day-explained-how-quantum-computing-threatens-today-s-cryptography-xdjedwwmp","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/rTM95-gZtOs/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":3,"created_at":"2026-04-30T11:01:24.000Z"},{"id":"E6o0pRzJz","title":"Is open source safe? Featuring Mixture of Experts","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PJGIWDW_W2A","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/is-open-source-safe-featuring-mixture-of-experts-e6o0przjz","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/PJGIWDW_W2A/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2026-04-29T10:00:42.000Z"},{"id":"Lywm47NYE","title":"What is a Supercomputer for AI? How GPUs Drive Machine Learning","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zocwmW5wZe8","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-is-a-supercomputer-for-ai-how-gpus-drive-machine-learning-lywm47nye","summary":"GPUs became the dominant hardware for AI because they excel at parallel mathematical operations and can hold large model weights in high-bandwidth memory \u2014 capabilities originally developed for video game graphics rendering. CPUs, by contrast, are general-purpose chips optimized for varied sequential tasks with less dedicated memory. The post explains the architectural differences between CPUs and GPUs (compute, cache, control, memory), why those differences matter for training and running LLMs, and when you actually need a GPU versus when a CPU can suffice \u2014 depending on model size, workload type, and whether the application is personal or customer-facing.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/zocwmW5wZe8/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-28T11:01:51.000Z"},{"id":"6e16sXJsl","title":"What is OpenClaw? Inside AI Agents, LLMs and the Agentic Loop","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L7FF8Zgab3M","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-is-openclaw-inside-ai-agents-llms-and-the-agentic-loop-6e16sxjsl","summary":"OpenClaw is a free, open-source AI agent that bridges the gap between LLMs knowing what to do and actually doing it. It runs as a local Node.js service using a hub-and-spoke architecture centered on a gateway that handles message routing, session management, and tool use. The agent operates on the ReAct pattern: reasoning over context, acting via tools (browser, terminal, APIs, skills), and observing results in a loop until a task is complete. Users interact through messaging platforms like Slack, iMessage, or Discord via adapters. Skills are markdown-based instruction files that extend the agent's capabilities on demand without flooding the context window. Security risks include misconfigured internet-exposed instances, prompt injection from untrusted inputs, and unsafe skill code \u2014 requiring isolated environments, credential encryption, and careful code review.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/L7FF8Zgab3M/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-27T11:00:36.000Z"},{"id":"TAmMDucTv","title":"Build, Reuse, or Hybrid? How Orchestration Powers Agentic AI","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tNQPNBQC5kg","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/build-reuse-or-hybrid-how-orchestration-powers-agentic-ai-tammductv","summary":"A conceptual walkthrough of three approaches to building agentic AI systems: building from scratch, reusing pre-built components, or combining both in a hybrid model. The central argument is that regardless of which path a team chooses, an orchestration layer is essential to bind agents together, manage task routing, enforce governance, handle tool invocation, and coordinate handoffs. A practical checklist is offered: list use cases, decide on build/reuse/hybrid, define the orchestration layer, then pilot and measure results.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/tNQPNBQC5kg/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-25T11:01:32.000Z"},{"id":"qZGLFftHg","title":"Apple\u2019s new CEO & how AI understands intent","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vCP7C8CVw28","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/apple-s-new-ceo-how-ai-understands-intent-qzglffthg","summary":"A podcast episode covering four AI and tech news stories: Apple's CEO transition from Tim Cook to John Ternus (a hardware-focused executive) and implications for Apple's AI strategy; Amazon's $5B investment in Anthropic (potentially rising to $25B) with Anthropic committing to $100B+ in AWS cloud services; insights from Adobe Summit on agentic AI orchestration and marketing workflows; and the leak of Anthropic's restricted Mythos model by a Discord group. Discussion touches on on-device vs cloud AI, AI hardware specialization (ASICs vs GPUs), how AI agents are changing consumer purchasing intent and advertising, and the forming of tight cloud-model provider alliances (Amazon/Anthropic, Microsoft/OpenAI).","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/vCP7C8CVw28/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-24T10:01:40.000Z"}],"top_posts":[{"id":"msjVWkyMk","title":"How to Build a Multi-agent AI System","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gUrENDkPw_k","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-build-a-multi-agent-ai-system-msjvwkymk","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/gUrENDkPw_k/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":38,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2024-08-15T11:00:46.000Z"},{"id":"xDJEDWwmp","title":"Q\u2011Day Explained: How Quantum Computing Threatens Today\u2019s Cryptography","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rTM95-gZtOs","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/q-day-explained-how-quantum-computing-threatens-today-s-cryptography-xdjedwwmp","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/rTM95-gZtOs/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":3,"created_at":"2026-04-30T11:01:24.000Z"},{"id":"tIDnPkawu","title":"The Power of Recurrent Neural Networks (RNN)","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Gafjk7_w1i8","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-power-of-recurrent-neural-networks-rnn--tidnpkawu","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Gafjk7_w1i8/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":20,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-09-26T15:36:25.000Z"},{"id":"NsJLTiQy4","title":"AI, Machine Learning, Deep Learning and Generative AI Explained","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qYNweeDHiyU","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ai-machine-learning-deep-learning-and-generative-ai-explained-nsjltiqy4","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/qYNweeDHiyU/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":18,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-08-05T11:00:52.000Z"},{"id":"7Y